+# DH first playable test build
+
+The user requested a subagent review followed by continued implementation until a
+playable build was available. Work remains local; upstream outreach is pending.
+This extends the earlier P1 stopping point. It does not mark S0–S2 or the full
+release gates complete.
+
+## Build and installation
+
+The local artifact is
+`/home/vox/projects/voxel-server-support/build/dh-playable/2026-10-01/lod-server-support-fabric-dh-playable-mc1.21.1.jar`.
+The same directory contains a validated sample client YAML, build receipt and test
+instructions. Use a separate test profile so its Voxy terrain cache can be discarded.
+
+1. Use Minecraft **1.21.1**, **Java 21** and Fabric. Replace the test profile's
+   existing LSS jar with this jar; keep one `lss` mod installed.
+2. Install the compatible Voxy/Sodium pair. The reference pair is
+   `voxy-0.2.15-beta-sodium0.8.12.jar` and
+   `sodium-fabric-0.8.13-beta.2+mc1.21.1.jar`. Fabric API is required.
+3. Remove the Distant Horizons mod from this test client. The adapter detects it
+   before channel registration and leaves DH mode unavailable when it is installed.
+4. For a fresh test profile, copy the supplied `lss-client-config.yaml` into its
+   `config` directory. For an existing YAML, merge the following into its `lod`
+   group, then run `/lss reload` and reconnect:
+
+   ```yaml
+   lod:
+     source: distant_horizons
+     receive: true
+     distance_chunks: 32
+     dh:
+       profile: dh_support_15
+       refresh_seconds: 120
+   ```
+
+5. Join a Paper 1.21.1 server running **DH Support 0.14.0**, using its default
+   FullBuilder with `dummy_chunk` disabled. LSS is not required on the server.
+6. Run `/lss dhstatus`. The status should move from waiting for config to acquiring
+   terrain, and its tile/column counters should increase. Keep vanilla render
+   distance below 32 chunks and look beyond vanilla terrain. Walk or fly to check
+   that acquisition follows your position. `/lss reset` drains DH conversion before
+   wiping Voxy and clears DH receipts so terrain is requested again.
+
+To return to native LSS, change `lod.source` to `lss`, reload and reconnect. Source
+and profile changes wait for reconnect; the refresh interval applies live. DH mode
+does not establish an LSS terrain, far-player or region-summary session. Use
+`/lss dhstatus` for this experimental source.
+
+## Implemented behavior
+
+- Optional Fabric client-only payload registration and bounded inbound ownership,
+  checked before allocation and before the loader queues its callback.
+- Exact config-before-level-init sequence, delayed until the client channel
+  announcement can reach Paper. One selected profile; no incompatible probing.
+- A worker for ordered framing, split assembly, decode and detached section
+  construction. Main-thread handoff checks world/session identity and vanilla
+  authority again. Only Voxy receives DH sections, under a DH-owned failure handle.
+- Session-only tile receipts. Untouched tiles are prioritized before incomplete
+  retries and accepted refreshes. Complete eligible columns are required before a
+  tile becomes fresh; unknown coverage cannot clear known terrain.
+- A conservative DH Support radius of 32 chunks and one generation request per
+  second, with at most one generation request outstanding. The manual column-rate
+  setting charges up to sixteen columns per tile. Official profiles prefer sync
+  timestamp zero, then bounded generation; their live gates remain pending.
+- Native cache buckets, including alias/world siblings, are invalidated before DH
+  handoff. Vanilla-held columns remain protected across reception pauses and reset.
+- Source/profile YAML settings, diagnostic command and DH-aware reset. This first
+  test build does not yet expose source/profile selectors in the Sodium page.
+
+Refresh deliberately requests full snapshots: no nonzero timestamp optimization
+is claimed before the family time-offset evidence is complete. Movement changes
+the next scan; already-sent same-world requests may finish. NeoForge transport,
+official server captures, native Windows rendering, custom-height live sessions,
+load comparisons and the full packaged gauntlet remain pending.
+
+## Review and validation
+
+The subagent found and verified fixes for fragment heap accounting, the missing
+development XZ runtime, bridge visibility, plugin border units, reset receipts,
+authority-cap containment, terminal cleanup and scheduler starvation. Its
+stationary-player simulation changed from 121/240 eligible tiles acquired after
+30 minutes to **240/240** with the revised scheduler. DH property resolution also
+handles unusual unknown values without passing through the native wire grammar.
+
+Java 21 checks passed:
+
+- **46** codec/session-policy tests, including the frozen captures and hostile
+  decoding/resource cases.
+- **148** settings tests, including reconnect-scoped source/profile and live refresh.
+- **88** native session/reset/converter tests. The converter verifies every captured
+  land voxel's block and light, solid terrain, state properties, actual minimum Y,
+  explicit no-sky light, incomplete coverage and unusual property fallback.
+- All **120** common main sources and the changed Fabric/shared client sources compile.
+- Release-check selftest: **124 cases** plus **9** SQLite packaging helper tests.
+- The actual remapped Fabric jar passes private codec/XZ ownership checks. Its
+  nested common jar loads settings without stock YAML/XZ on the classpath and
+  decodes both frozen tiles to their previously independently derived hashes.
+
+This session cannot start Gradle's socket service or bind a loopback listener
+(`PermissionError: Operation not permitted`). The jar was assembled from the
+pinned 0.16.0+mc1.21.1 baseline, Java-21 compiled changes, private relocated XZ and
+the cached named-to-intermediary mappings. Its SQLite capsule is byte-identical.
+The assembler pins the baseline hash and writes class/artifact hashes to its receipt.
+This is a local incremental development build; a normal Gradle build and a new live
+client/server/render test have **not** passed in this session.
+
+The earlier water-only display issue remains a separate WSL D3D12/NVIDIA finding.
+The captured terrain contains solids and the earlier llvmpipe control renders them.
+For a WSL software control, use `GALLIUM_DRIVER=llvmpipe`,
+`MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=4.6` and `MESA_GLSL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=460`; omit the GPU
+adapter override. No NVIDIA or native Windows graphics fix is claimed.
+
+Evidence: `docs/planning/evidence/dh-playable-2026-10-01/`. Implementation remains
+uncommitted on `feat/dh-codec-p1-mc1.21.1` in `.worktrees/dh-client-p1`.
